1
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:05,757
In Curio's lab, Noah brings a magnet closer…

2
00:00:05,807 --> 00:00:06,132
click!

3
00:00:06,182 --> 00:00:07,948
The paper clips jump onto it.

4
00:00:07,998 --> 00:00:10,691
How does it do that, without touching them?

5
00:00:11,529 --> 00:00:14,551
So Mila tries everything: a key, hop!

6
00:00:14,601 --> 00:00:15,547
A nail, hop!

7
00:00:15,597 --> 00:00:19,449
But the copper coin, the cork, the plastic toy…

8
00:00:19,499 --> 00:00:20,661
nothing moves.

9
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:22,966
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:25,482 --> 00:00:26,037
Mini mode!

11
00:00:26,087 --> 00:00:28,763
Around the magnet there is an invisible zone…

12
00:00:28,813 --> 00:00:29,913
the magnetic field.

13
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:32,517
It is strongest at the two ends, the poles,

14
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:34,627
and it goes through air and paper.

15
00:00:35,482 --> 00:00:37,915
Iron is full of tiny magnets in a jumble.

16
00:00:37,965 --> 00:00:39,973
When the magnet comes closer, hop,

17
00:00:40,023 --> 00:00:41,547
they line up the same way!

18
00:00:41,597 --> 00:00:43,303
So the iron becomes a magnet,

19
00:00:43,353 --> 00:00:44,564
and it is pulled in.

20
00:00:45,382 --> 00:00:47,621
But in copper, gold or plastic,

21
00:00:47,671 --> 00:00:49,394
no tiny magnets line up.

22
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:51,314
So the magnet has no grip…

23
00:00:51,364 --> 00:00:52,398
nothing moves.

24
00:00:53,174 --> 00:00:54,042
And two magnets?

25
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:55,649
Same pole against same pole,

26
00:00:55,699 --> 00:00:57,140
they push each other away.

27
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:58,288
But turn one around…

28
00:00:58,338 --> 00:00:59,944
clack, they grab each other!

29
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:03,249
And that's how a magnet attracts metal.

30
00:01:04,289 --> 00:01:06,844
The magnet lines up the tiny magnets inside iron:

31
00:01:06,894 --> 00:01:09,607
the iron becomes a magnet too, and it is pulled in.

32
00:01:10,402 --> 00:01:11,110
With an adult:

33
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:14,633
put paper clips on a sheet of paper and move a magnet underneath…

34
00:01:14,683 --> 00:01:16,204
they slide all by themselves!

35
00:01:16,254 --> 00:01:17,934
But a copper coin doesn't move.

36
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,863
And what is hidden inside the Earth?

37
00:01:20,913 --> 00:01:22,143
The answer tomorrow.
